                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Second half of the nineteenth-century script.</seg>
                           <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                         <desc> Careful, regular, by a well-trained hand. Despite the initial impression that
                           parts of the text were written by a different hand, it seems to be
                           incorrect. Difference in the quality of the handwriting (finer letters with
                           more space between them and more massive letters placed closer to one another)
                           may be due to the fact that the scribe used different
                           pens. The scribe is <persName role="scribe" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15353GabraSellase"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Gabra Śǝllāse</persName> (see <ref target="#coloph1"/>).</desc>
                      
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; incipits and headings of the texts
                           (sometimes alternately in black and red lines); the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">mǝʿrāf</foreign>, numbers,
                           x-shaped signs and incipits of the chapters; elements of punctuation marks and Ethiopic numerals; names of the donor and scribe. On
                           the opening page of each Gospel, a few lines are rubricated (in groups of two lines, alternating with black lines).</seg>
                     </handNote>
                     
                     <handNote xml:id="h2" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Second half of the nineteenth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                        <desc>Mediocre handwriting; angular shape of the letters, slightly slanted to the right. The hand executed the ‘tituli’ and <ref target="#a1"/>. 
                           Most likely he also introduced a number of omitted words and passages as well as numbers of sections.</desc>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; elements of punctuation marks and Ethiopic numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <decoDesc>

                     <decoNote type="band" xml:id="d1">
                        <locus target="#15ra"/>
                        <desc>Three horizontal chains of red and black dots connected with six vertical chains of similar dots.</desc></decoNote>
                  </decoDesc>
                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus from="2ra" to="3vb"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4329Andemta">ʾAndǝmtā</title> of selected episodes from the Gospels (the miracle of the five loaves and two fish,
                              the washing of the disciples’ feet, the denial of Peter and Christ’s resurrection from the dead), as told by different Evangelists. 
                              The text is written in Amharic by a mediocre hand.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="am"/>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus from="17va" to="17vb"/>
                           <desc type="DonationNote">Donation note written by <ref type="hand" target="#h2">Hand 2</ref>. It states that the codex was donated to 
                              <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0105DD">the sanctuary of ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</placeName> by <persName role="patron" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15349AskalaMaryam"><roleName type="title">Mamhǝr</roleName> ʾAskāla Māryām</persName>, 
                              (spiritual) son of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15350WaldaAbiyaE"><roleName type="title">ʾAbuna</roleName>Walda ʿAbiya ʾƎgziʾ</persName>. Two other people are mentioned: 
                              his (spiritual) brother  <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15351GabraIyasus"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Gabra ʾIyasus</persName>, and his (spiritual) son 
                              <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15352TaklaMaryam">Takla Māryām</persName>. 
                           </desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">ዝንቱ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ ለመምህር፡ አስካለ፡ ማርያም፡
                              ወልዱ፡ ለአቡነ፡ ወልደ፡ ዓቢየእግዚእ፡ ዘአስረፀ፡ አክናፈ፡ ከመ፡ መላእክት፡ ዘርእዮ፡ ግኁስ፡ ባህታዊ፡
                              በዋልባ፡ ወወሀቦ፡ ለመቅደሰ፡ አቡነ፡ አረጋዊ፡ ከመ፡ ይኩኖ፡ መድኀኒተ፡ ሥጋ፡ ወነፍስ፡ ወእኁሁ፡ አባ፡ ገብረ፡
                              ኢየሱስ፡ ወለወልዱ፡ ተክለ፡ (vb) ማርያም፤ ኦአበውየ፡ ወአኃውየ፡ ኢትርስዑነ፡ ፩፩፡ አቡነ፡ ዘበሰማያት፡
                              በጊዜ፡ ቅዳሴ፡ ወጸሎት፡ ካህናተ፡ ደም፡ ልዕልት፡ ዳግሚት፡ ሰማይ፡ ማኅደረ፡ ትጉሃን፡ መላእክት፡ ዘኃረያ፡
                              አረጋዊ፡ ጸባዖት፡ በስብሐት፡ ወበውዳሴ፡ ኅጽርት፨</q>
                           <q xml:lang="en">This book (belongs) to Mamhǝr ʾAskāla Māryām, son of ʾAbuna Walda ʿAbiya ʾƎgziʾ,
                              who spread out (his) wings like angels, which was seen by a secluded
                              hermit in Wāl(dǝ)bbā, and (who) donated it to the sanctuary of ʾAbuna
                              ʾAragāwi, so that it may be for him the salvation of (his) body and
                              soul; and (to) his brother ʾAbbā Gabra ʾIyasus, and to his son Takla
                              Māryām. Oh my fathers and my brothers, do not forget us, each one (of
                              you say) Paternoster at the time of the Mass and the prayer – (you)
                              priests of Dāmmo, the exalted, the second heaven, the abode of the
                              watchful angels, which ʾAragāwi has chosen, fenced off (by angelic)
                              hosts, by praise and by laudation.</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <locus target="#1r"/>
                           <desc>The name of the work in written in large letters: <foreign xml:lang="gez">4ቱ ወንጌል</foreign>.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e2">
                           <locus target="#1r"/>
                           <desc>The internal number of the of the monastic library, 310, is written in bottom right corner of the folium.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e3">
                           <locus target="#5ra"/>
                           <desc>Shelfmark C3-IV-237</desc>
                        </item>
                       
                        <item xml:id="e4">
                           <locus target="#19v #41ra #43r #46r #110r"/> 
                           <desc type="Correction">Numerous corrections of the text: added omitted passages by a single hand, most likely  in <ref target="#h2">Hand 2</ref>. The folia listed above are a few examples.</desc>
                        </item>
                             
                        <item xml:id="e5">
                              <locus target="#46r #185v"/>
                           <desc>(in the upper margin) Crude notes.</desc>
                        </item>
                       
                     </list>
                  </additions>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <binding contemporary="true">
                        <decoNote xml:id="b1">Two wooden boards.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b2" type="Cover">Dark brown <term key="tooling" ana="#tooling">blind tooled</term> leather; <term key="textileInlay" ana="#textileInlay">textile inlays</term>.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b3" type="Sewing">Two pairs of sewing stations.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b4" type="SewingStations">4</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b5" type="bindingMaterial">
                           <material key="wood"/>
                           <material key="leather"/>
                           <material key="textile"/>
                        </decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b6" type="Endbands">Present.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b7" type="Other">Two pairs of chain endband stitches on the spine cover. White and coloured <term key="leafStringMark" ana="#leafStringMark">threads</term> are inserted in the
                           right upper corner of <locus target="#21r"/> and outer margins of some other folia.</decoNote>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
               </physDesc>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origPlace>
                        <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</placeName>
                     </origPlace>
                     <origDate when="1891">According to the colophon, the manuscript 
                        was completed in <date calendar="world" when-custom="7383" notBefore="1890" notAfter="1891">‘the year of the world’ 7383 (= 1890/91 A.D.)</date>. Additional
                        data in the colophon (the <foreign xml:lang="gez">maṭqǝʿ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾabaqte</foreign>, the year of the Evangelist
                        Luke) correspond to <date when="1891">1891 A.D.</date>.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance>The commissioner of the manuscript is <persName role="patron" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15349AskalaMaryam"><roleName type="title">Mamhǝr</roleName> ʾAskāla Māryām</persName> (mentioned in the
                     supplication formulas on <locus target="#68rb #96va #97rb #149rb"/>, in <ref target="#coloph1"/>, and in <ref target="#a1"/>). <ref target="#a1"/> also mentions his spiritual father
                     <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15350WaldaAbiyaE"><roleName type="title">ʾAbuna</roleName>Walda ʿAbiya ʾƎgziʾ</persName>, 
                     his (spiritual) brother  <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15351GabraIyasus"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Gabra ʾIyasus</persName>, and his (spiritual) son 
                     <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15352TaklaMaryam">Takla Māryām</persName>.</provenance>
               </history>
